<p>I agree 100%. Obviously they're not just gonna let her hold onto the damn crocodile if it might be the real SCP, but it's easier to just steal it &amp; replace it while she sleeps and keep her friendly to them.</p>
<p>I also feel like I need more of a sense of what's going on behind the scenes. Why this particular little girl? Why this particular crocodile? Why does she like racing? I like that she is super normal and seems pretty well-adjusted (a refreshing change of pace from the endless parade of mutilated and / or traumatized kids you typically see on here) but I still think it needs more backstory to it, even if that backstory is just a few lines that you gesture toward in the actual text. Right now she's just another mutant at Professor X's School for Gifted Youngsters, a weird thing because we're on a site full of weird things and that's where she goes, and I'm kinda bored by that.</p>

